Buat Zynakal 

Sampai bila;
Mau jadi nakal.

Luka lamamu itu;
Bukan sia-sia;
Sejarah dukamu itu;
Lebih pahit dari hempedu.

Namun jika tindak tandukmu;
Penuh hikmah pesona luhur;
Dengan izin-Nya pasti..
Zynakal hatimu menguntum mekar;
Tidak ramaipun yang sedar;
Dirimu ibarat..
Padi merunduk berisi tawaduk teduh;
Embun menitis sentuh jiwa yang patuh.

Aku berdoa..
Moga Engkau terus berlari jauh;
Terbang gemilang walau pancaroba merusuh;
Terus diredhai ke kerajaan kekal tiada runtuh. 🤲

@17:35 controversial take, this is a selfish take but a wheelchair is a need, some people require wheelchairs to move around like they cannot avoid. holding your sleeping child is a choice, its not a need. just because they fit on that stop, doesn't mean the next stop won't have a wheelchair. i'd understand if its one person and a stroller, like shes pregnant or she has another child but this was a capable family. i don't think anyone will say anything about a single parent because i moved and made way but this doesn't mean every priority will be given to a family on public transport, especially when wheelchair users have had to make way for strollers which shouldn't even be a thing. 

not to play devil's advocate but if its so hard for one parent, this is exactly what private hires and taxis are for. In a way folding the stroller is etiquette because we all didn’t make the choice for you to have a child. But while bus employees should have a kinder approach and just explain how the crowd would be i think some people also should stop feeling entitled to a public space in general, it’s hard to ask for compassion when it’s not given first

Because of this, wheelchair users are being told to wait for the next bus. This isn’t the a problem of space its choice and need. Wheelchair users HAVE NO choice. And parents should be aware they need to make space for those users. The accessible bus was made for wheelchairs and not strollers in mind. Case by case but sometimes parents feel entitled because they have a child to begin with which shouldn’t be the case anyway.

